From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:19:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virgl: pass PIPE_BIND_LINEAR to the host

pipe_to_virgl_bind() drops PIPE_BIND_LINEAR, so a buffer a client
allocates with gbm SCANOUT | LINEAR reaches virglrenderer as a plain
scanout resource, and the host gives it the layout its GL driver
picks: BROADCOM_UIF on the Raspberry Pi 5's V3D. The guest compositor
puts such a buffer on a plane (virtio-gpu has no modifiers, so to the
guest it is linear), and the host compositor cannot scan the tiled
texture out, so it composes it with the GPU.

Pass the bit on as VIRGL_BIND_LINEAR, which virgl_hw.h defines.
With virglrenderer's 0024 the host then allocates the resource as a
linear gbm bo. The AAOS tree's newer Mesa has the same function
without the line.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/virgl/virgl_resource.h
@@ -149,6 +149,8 @@
       outbind |= VIRGL_BIND_SCANOUT;
    if (pbind & PIPE_BIND_SHARED)
       outbind |= VIRGL_BIND_SHARED;
+   if (pbind & PIPE_BIND_LINEAR)
+      outbind |= VIRGL_BIND_LINEAR;
    if (pbind & PIPE_BIND_SHADER_BUFFER)
       outbind |= VIRGL_BIND_SHADER_BUFFER;
    if (pbind & PIPE_BIND_QUERY_BUFFER)
